From 14ffdc6344901eb81dab49071a6b459ffbcbd5a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@brenup.dev>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix production build failure and revert broken OBE wiring in
 lesson builder

Root causes of the failed deploy (commit 5ee9e64):

1. react/no-unescaped-entities build error in LessonBlockPreview.tsx.
   The IMAGE_TEXT work accidentally replaced curly quote characters
   around the QUOTE block body with raw straight quotes, which Next's
   ESLint rules reject at build time. Restored as HTML entities.

2. TypeScript error in app/admin/lessons/[id]/builder/page.tsx.
   That same commit began wiring Codex's outcome-based-education (OBE)
   data into the lesson builder page (fetching lesson_outcomes,
   course_outcomes, assessment_items, learning_skills, etc. and
   passing an obe prop into LessonBuilderWorkspace), but never
   finished: LessonBuilderWorkspace Props type was never updated to
   accept obe, so the build failed a type check. Separately, and
   more importantly, Codex migration 024_outcome_based_education.sql
   has not been applied to the live database yet (last applied
   migration is 015), so those queries would have thrown at runtime
   against tables that do not exist even if the type error were
   silenced. Reverted this page back to only fetching what
   LessonBuilderWorkspace actually uses. This does not touch any of
   Codex files (app/admin/obe/actions.ts, lib/obe.ts,
   types/obe.types.ts, components/LessonOutcomeManager.tsx,
   AssessmentMetadataEditor.tsx, CourseQuizOutcomeMapper.tsx,
   ObeActionForm.tsx, or the migration) - they remain exactly as
   Codex left them, ready to be wired in once the migration ships.

3. Restored the outcomes textarea save path in
   updateLessonBuilderDetails that was silently dropped in the same
   abandoned integration attempt.

Also removed stray files accidentally committed alongside the
IMAGE_TEXT work: old patch files, add_image_text.sh, duplicate stale
root-level LoginForm.tsx and layout.tsx, and two vim swap files.

Verified with a full npm run build - compiles and type-checks clean.
