-From 86f2eb3acc1180e019dd9709e3ba9efa8660df3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <assistant@brenup.dev>
-Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:06:46 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] Make A1-A2/B1-B2/C1-C2/All Levels official lesson & course
- levels
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Root cause of the crash: the lesson builder settings UI offered combined-
-range levels (A1-A2, B1-B2, C1-C2, All Levels) in its level dropdown, but
-the server-side Zod schema validating the save (lessonSchema /
-builderLessonSchema in app/admin/lessons/actions.ts) only accepted the
-six base CEFR bands. Picking a combined range and saving threw an
-uncaught ZodError on the server, surfacing as the
-'Application error: a server-side exception has occurred' page.
-
-This was also inconsistent more broadly: the combined ranges had only
-been added to 4 of the ~15 places a lesson/course level appears, so even
-once a lesson was saved with e.g. 'A1-A2' it would render incorrectly or
-become unfindable elsewhere (edit page dropdown, public lessons grid
-filter/sort/theme, course-by-level counts on the public courses page).
-
-Fix:
-- Add lib/levels.ts as the single source of truth: CEFR_LEVELS (the 6
-  base bands, used by the unrelated learner placement-test cefr_level,
-  which is intentionally left untouched), CONTENT_LEVELS (all 10 values
-  a lesson/course level can hold), a shared sort-order map, and an
-  anchorCefrLevel() helper for anywhere that needs to collapse a content
-  level down to its nearest single CEFR band.
-- Widen lessonSchema's level enum in app/admin/lessons/actions.ts to
-  CONTENT_LEVELS — this is the actual fix for the crash.
-- Replace every duplicated inline level array (lesson builder, new
-  lesson form, lesson edit form, course builder, admin courses list)
-  with the shared CONTENT_LEVELS constant so they can't drift again.
-- Widen the lesson edit page's level dropdown (previously stuck at 6
-  options, silently unable to display/save a lesson already tagged with
-  a combined range).
-- Extend LessonsGrid's public filter chips, sort order, and color theme
-  map to cover the combined ranges and All Levels, with a sane neutral
-  fallback theme for All Levels.
-- Extend the public /courses page's per-level count breakdown
-  (levelOrder) so courses tagged with a combined range or All Levels are
-  actually counted instead of silently dropped.
-- courses/actions.ts: swapped a hardcoded 'All Levels' string literal
-  for the shared ALL_LEVELS_LABEL constant.
-
-Explicitly NOT touched, and why:
-- Quiz level dropdowns/schema (AdminQuizBuilder, QuizVisualBuilder,
-  QuizzesGrid, admin/quizzes/actions.ts): combined ranges were never
-  exposed there, so nothing is broken; left at the 6 base bands.
-- LevelTestAdminWorkspace.tsx / admin/level-test/actions.ts: these are
-  CEFR placement-test bands used for scoring thresholds, a different
-  concept from a content level tag — widening them would corrupt the
-  test's percentage-band math.
-- app/account/page.tsx and app/page.tsx CEFR progress bars: driven by
-  profiles.cefr_level, a real Postgres enum representing the learner's
-  own placement-test result, not a content tag. Left at 6 bands.
-- components/NewLessonForm.tsx: confirmed dead code, not imported
-  anywhere; left untouched.
